<title>USA: JORDAN BUYS 50,000 T U.S. HRW WHEAT FOR OCT-TRADE.</title>
<headline>JORDAN BUYS 50,000 T U.S. HRW WHEAT FOR OCT-TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jordan bought overnight 50,000 tonnes of U.S. hard red winter wheat for October shipment, several U.S. exporters said.  </p>
<p>&quot;They passed on 50,000 tonnes they were tendering for November,&quot; one U.S. exporter said. &quot;I don't know the flat price but I heard it was something like 25 (cents) over the KCBT December contract, FOB.&quot;</p>
<p>Wheat for December delivery on the Kansas City Baard of Trade settled at $3.89-3/4 a bushel on Monday.</p>
<p>((--Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
